From: Siddhant Modi <siddhant.modi@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: sensor: lsm6dsl: add motion (wake-up) trigger

Add SENSOR_TRIG_MOTION, raised by the chip's wake-up function: the slope
of the acceleration exceeding a threshold. SENSOR_ATTR_SLOPE_TH sets the
threshold (in steps of 1/64 of the accelerometer's full scale) and
SENSOR_ATTR_SLOPE_DUR the samples it must last. The wake-up interrupt is
routed to INT1 while a motion handler is set, so INT1 can also wake a SoC
from a low-power state.

Interrupt sources are now routed to INT1 only while their trigger has a
handler. Data-ready was routed at init, which kept INT1 toggling at the
data rate even with no data-ready handler, and would hide motion events.
With both triggers set, the status registers tell the two apart.

Also fix the misspelt LSM6DSL_SHIFT_WAKE_UP_DUR_WAKE_DUR, and add an I2C
emulator (wake-up events, register access) with a test of the triggers
and attributes on native_sim.

